# Pull requests

## Base branch

**Always open PRs against `dev`.** Never use `main` as the PR base in this repository.

When using `gh pr create`, always pass `--base dev`.

## Author paragraph (required before drafting)

When the user asks to create or open a pull request:

1. **Stop and ask** for a short paragraph in the user's own words explaining what the PR does and what it contains. Do not draft the full PR or run `gh pr create` until they provide it.
2. After they reply, draft the rest of the PR using their paragraph at the top of the body (see format below).
3. Then push if needed and create the PR.

## PR body format

```markdown
<Author paragraph — paste or lightly edit the user's words; do not replace with generic agent prose.>

## Summary

- …
- …

## Test plan

- [ ] …
```

## Git commands

- Use `git log dev..HEAD` and `git diff dev...HEAD` (not `main`) to understand what the PR will include.
- Follow the repo's existing PR title style from recent merged PRs on `dev`.
